		{"id":"427bcabd6085fed4","type":"text","text":"Takeaways","x":13481,"y":256,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"7594affa38a74a5c","type":"link","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_6SQPc961ZE&t=1s","x":10598,"y":-876,"width":640,"height":360},
		{"id":"c7e40e162b57a139","type":"text","text":"Liquids:\n* Bulk of a liquid is represented using grid of voxels (Eulerian approach)\n* Top part (e.g., waves, foam, etc.) is represented using points (Lagrangian)","x":-1403,"y":1480,"width":320,"height":288},
		{"id":"f3f5caeb20e84d2b","type":"file","file":"Images/Dynamics2/NVIDIA_GVDB_FluidSim.jpg","x":-1380,"y":2487,"width":446,"height":292},
		{"id":"15b37370c31e7c24","type":"file","file":"Images/Dynamics2/NVIDIA_GVDB_FluidSim_Liquid_Animation2.jpg","x":-1640,"y":2819,"width":704,"height":294},
		{"id":"e788f3a9ceb0d8c1","type":"text","text":"**Physically-based simulation**\n* Volumes/grids: Eulerian\n* Particles/points: Lagrangian\n* Hybrid: voxels and particles, e.g. FLIP: https://matthias-research.github.io/pages/tenMinutePhysics/18-flip.pdf","x":-2232,"y":866,"width":680,"height":210},
		{"id":"b287b66f12d74672","type":"text","text":"Fluid modeling","x":-2017,"y":1164,"width":250,"height":63},
		{"id":"46f21c61a01b5a53","type":"file","file":"Images/Dynamics2/Entagma.png","x":-2526,"y":2437,"width":361,"height":281},
		{"id":"c10ae30e92247a12","type":"text","text":"**Particles and volumes similarities:**\n* Both can be used to represent fuzzy objects\n* Both can be used to describe geometry in-between surfaces or inside surfaces\n\n**Particles and volumes differences:**\n* If very sparse geometry or eye-visible geometry is being modeled (e.g., leafs, snow, rain, etc.) then particles are more efficient\n* If large amount of eye-invisible particles are being modeled (e.g., fog, clouds, smoke, etc.) then volumes are more efficient.\n\n**Particles and volumes for modeling:**\n* Volume of space can be used to store vector field generated using noise, curves or vectors on surface (e.g., tangent field)\n\t* Volume vector field can be used to advect particles in particle system\n* Dynamics of volumetric media can be modeled using physically based methods directly on grid of voxels. \n\t* Result can be converted to particles\n\t* Vector fields computed during simulation can be used as driving force for particles\n* More artistic simulation of volumetric media can be performed using particles and particle system\n\t* Resulting particles can be converted to volume. Example: artistic cloud morphing is easier to perform with a help of particle system than directly using physically based methods.","x":-2297,"y":3216,"width":1187,"height":630},
		{"id":"aefba5454b73d8cf","type":"file","file":"Images/Dynamics2/NVIDIA_GVDB_FluidSim_Gas.jpg","x":-2524,"y":2972,"width":359,"height":176},
		{"id":"8156a716b40009d7","type":"file","file":"Images/Dynamics2/NVIDIA_GVDB_FluidSim_GasShaded.jpg","x":-2524,"y":2758,"width":357,"height":172},
		{"id":"0e05d5f0117ebcc5","type":"file","file":"Images/Dynamics2/NVIDIA_GVDB_FluidSim_Liquid_Animation.jpg","x":-2083,"y":2819,"width":400,"height":294},
		{"id":"1de8ea6a08c7c7dc","type":"file","file":"Images/Dynamics2/NVIDIA_GVDB_FluidSim_Liquid.jpg","x":-2081,"y":2487,"width":663,"height":292},
		{"id":"b5006b0346660b7b","type":"text","text":"Gas:\n* Each voxel contains density and color information (Eulerian approach, since describing gas with particles is unnecessary expensive)","x":-2342,"y":1480,"width":290,"height":288},
		{"id":"526ea5e73bda6eac","type":"text","text":"Static, e.g. static cloud:\n* Density and color information inside voxels is generated using noise","x":-2504,"y":1898,"width":272,"height":211},
		{"id":"19fd5b4578329bbb","type":"file","file":"Images/Dynamics2/GridParticleSim2.jpg","x":-1866,"y":1679,"width":400,"height":178},
		{"id":"9fe965ed6e70afd1","type":"file","file":"Images/Dynamics2/GridParticleSim3.jpg","x":-1866,"y":1898,"width":400,"height":226},
		{"id":"16210d796b24e3c3","type":"text","text":"Dynamics, e.g., smoke:\n* Simulation is performed on voxels which determines density and color information stored per voxel","x":-2197,"y":1898,"width":292,"height":211},
		{"id":"3f93652e8de2ccae","type":"text","text":"Baking simulation at certain frame gives us possibility to store (freeze) resulting geometry as static.","x":-2176,"y":2174,"width":250,"height":187},
		{"id":"b9c6423c82091101","type":"text","text":"After simulation is finished, voxel/particle representation is triangulated and rendered","x":-1376,"y":1878,"width":266,"height":133},
		{"id":"0b7b70bcc846ea42","type":"file","file":"Images/Dynamics2/GridParticleSim.jpg","x":-1865,"y":1480,"width":399,"height":177}
	],
